Z||000004||turbo86se||12-04-2000||08:14 PM||||Hey Todd, <BR>Those are 16" Team Loco wheels, type 182 (I think) with Anthracite centers. I got them from Tire Rack. I've got 225/50/16 on the rear, and 205/55/16 up front. Delivered to my door in two days, mounted and balanced. I LOVE THOSE WHEELS!!!!<BR>Relatively speaking they weren't too much money. <P>Zuesrecking has some really good pics of the wheels. He's around here somewhere. <P>I don't mind if you duplicate the car at all, you'd have to do the turbo though, and the mint leather seats, woodgrain trim.....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I've got some ideas for what I'm doing next!!<P>If you go to Robertvol's website, NorthFL southGA, and click on joel's cars with bonus pics, there are some really good pics of my SE. Can't figure out how to post them here though.. <P>Thanks for the compliments guys!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||82-T/A||12-05-2000||08:47 AM||||Thanks! I think I'll probably get those.<P>My Fiero is medium metallic red right now... <P>Damn, I don't know what I want to do... this is soo frustrating.<P>I've got Two Fieros, neither of which I really want. <P>I WANT a 1985 Fiero GT 4-Speed like I used to have. <P>But... I bought the 1984 Fiero 2m4 SE that I have simply because this woman was going to junk it becuase it didn't pass Florida inspection. We don't have it anymore, but I fixed it anyway.. a cracked valve. But otherwise the car looks like it just came off the showroom floor. So I saved that one. The other Fiero, well, it was my first car.<P>I gave the 1984 Fiero 2m4 SE to my mom. I'm going to be rebuilding the suspension sometime this winter. But she has that to drive around when she doesn't want to drive her new Volvo 850 Turbo Wagon. And actually, she prefers the Fiero. So that worked out good.<P>I'm hoping I can give my 1987 Fiero SE / V6 to my dad after I'm done with the motor.. that way I'd be free and clear of any obligations of the car. It would always stay in the immediate family, I could always visit them (the cars)... AND I could focus on finding the right 1985 Fiero GT 4-Speed for me.... <P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||1
